B.a2Q=new A.aP("HISTORY OF THE SCHOOL",null,B.jL,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.Ja=new A.vK(1,B.v,null)
B.a3s=new A.aP("Krobo Girls' Presbyterian Secondary School is situated at the Western part of Odumase Krobo, about one kilometer off the Odumase - Assesewa road. It started as Krobo Girls' Middle School, which was founded by few female Scottish Missionaries in March, 1927 namely, Madam Sussie F. Lamont, Esther B. Harris and Catherine P. Moir. Under the Accelerated Plan of the government of Ghana, a two - year Teacher Training College for women was added to the Girls school in 1944 on experimental basis.\n\nThe College was constituted as a Certificate B Teacher Training College for women in 1951 under Ms. J.C Forman and the Management of the Presbyterian Church of Ghana.\n\nIn 1962, the two Year Teacher Training College changed to a four year certificate \"A\" Teacher Training College for women of which the very first Ghanaian Principal, Ms. Vida Annor Kwakye took over from Madam J.C Forman.\n\nIn September, 1973, the Krobo Girls Middle School phased out while Krobo Training College (Presbyterian) was converted to a Girls Secondary School, under the consolidation of Teacher Education Programme by the Ministry of Education. The school was then headed by Mrs. Agnes Akoto, the first Ghanaian Headmistress from 1973 to 1998. The school has been a Senior Secondary School in view of the then Educational Reforms by the Ministry of Education since January 1990 and 2007 Senior High School under the current educational reform.\n\nMrs. Gladys Kabuki Appiah took over from Mrs. Agnes Akoto after she had been the head for close to 26 years. Mrs. Gladys K. Appiah was made the head of the school from 1998 to 2009 when she was appointed Principal of Agogo Teacher's Training College. Then Madam Cecilia Obenewa Appiah took over then Mrs. Betty Aduhene Chinbuah. Currently Mrs. Bernice Noel Mensah Akutteh is the Headmistress and an Old Girl of the school.\n\nThe school is a Government Assisted Senior High School. The school offers General Science, Business, Visual Arts, Home Economics and General Arts.\n\nThe mission of the school is to deliver quality and holistic education, based on the Presbyterian Discipline and traditions that seems to prepare and equip the girl child for a full life both mentally and spiritually. Its purpose is to discipline not only the mind and body but also the spirit.",null,B.Dv,null,null,!0,null,null,null,null)
